From 3c1aad218f8bcbed7a20f6fdff59dd96dc670666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:53:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/av1dec: use sw_pix_fmt for film grain subsampling

The native AV1 decoder exports film grain parameters for
hardware-accelerated output.  Deriving their chroma subsampling from
frame->format uses the hardware pixel-format descriptor rather than
the stream's chroma layout.

For CUDA and CUARRAY output, this exports 0/0 instead of 1/1 for a
4:2:0 stream.  After downloading to a 4:2:0 software frame and copying
the frame properties, av_film_grain_params_select() rejects the entry
because its chroma subsampling does not match.

Use avctx->sw_pix_fmt to derive the exported chroma subsampling from
the negotiated software format.

Signed-off-by: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>

(cherry picked from commit 3c1aad218f8bcbed7a20f6fdff59dd96dc670666)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/3c1aad218f8bcbed7a20f6fdff59dd96dc670666
---
 libavcodec/av1dec.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/av1dec.c b/libavcodec/av1dec.c
index 315828e..e6512cd 100644
--- a/libavcodec/av1dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/av1dec.c
@@ -1072,7 +1072,9 @@ static int export_film_grain(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *frame)
 {
     AV1DecContext *s = avctx->priv_data;
     const AV1RawFilmGrainParams *film_grain = &s->cur_frame.film_grain;
-    const AVPixFmtDescriptor *pixdesc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(frame->format);
+    /* Use the negotiated software format for chroma subsampling,
+     * since frame->format may be a hardware pixel format. */
+    const AVPixFmtDescriptor *pixdesc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(avctx->sw_pix_fmt);
     AVFilmGrainParams *fgp;
     AVFilmGrainAOMParams *aom;
 
